---
title: "Achievements"
description: "Turn meaningful participation into milestones and rewards."
featureKey: "community.achievements"
permalink: "/modules/roles-and-progression/achievements/"
---
{% set feature = helperDocs.byKey[featureKey] %}
<h1>{{ feature.title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">{{ feature.summary }}</p>
<div class="status-row"><span class="status status-{{ feature.maturity }}">{{ feature.statusLabel }}</span></div>
{% if feature.maturity == 'blocked' %}<div class="notice notice-warning"><strong>Not currently available.</strong> This page describes the planned experience and its dependencies. There is no activation or publishing action today; details may change before release.</div>{% endif %}

<section class="card">
  <h2>Recommended setup</h2>
  {% if feature.maturity == 'blocked' %}
  <p>The planned flow will begin with a guided setup and a preview. It will not publish anything until the required provider, review, or contract is available.</p>
  {% else %}
  <ol class="steps"><li>Open the Helper panel for the selected server.</li><li>Review the permissions and preflight result.</li><li>Choose the recommended defaults, simulate the change, and publish only after the preview is correct.</li></ol>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<details class="docs-reference-details"><summary>Requirements and permissions</summary>
  <ul class="check-list">{% for permission in feature.permissions %}<li>{{ permission }}</li>{% else %}<li>Permissions will be shown here when the adapter requires them.</li>{% endfor %}{% for intent in feature.intents %}<li>Discord intent: {{ intent }}</li>{% endfor %}{% for dependency in feature.dependencies %}<li>Dependency: {{ dependency }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</details>

<details class="docs-reference-details"><summary>Behaviour and when to use it</summary>
  <h2>What this does</h2><p>{{ feature.summary }}</p>
  <h3>When to use it</h3><p>Use this module when you want a clear, server-scoped way to {{ feature.title | lower }}. Start with the recommended setup, then open advanced options only when you know what you need.</p>
</details>

<section class="card"><h2>Commands</h2>
{% if feature.commands and feature.commands.length %}<ul>{% for command in feature.commands %}<li><code>{{ command.name or command }}</code></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}<p>This module is configured from the panel; no public command is listed in the technical manifest.</p>{% endif %}
</section>

<details class="docs-reference-details"><summary>Preview, health and rollback</summary>
  <p>{% if feature.capabilities.simulation %}Use the panel simulation to see the matched rules and expected effects before publishing.{% else %}A simulation is not currently exposed for this module.{% endif %} {% if feature.capabilities.health %}The panel also reports health and dependency problems.{% endif %} {% if feature.capabilities.rollback %}Published revisions can be reverted without deleting history.{% endif %}</p>
  <dl class="technical-list"><dt>Adapter</dt><dd><code>{{ feature.adapter }}</code></dd><dt>Capabilities</dt><dd>{% for item, enabled in feature.capabilities %}{{ item }}{% if enabled %} enabled{% else %} unavailable{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd><dt>Schema version</dt><dd>{{ feature.schemaVersion }}</dd><dt>Source commit</dt><dd><code>{{ helperDocs.sourceCommit }}</code></dd></dl>
</details>

<details class="docs-reference-details"><summary>Common problems and recovery</summary>
  <ul><li>If the panel reports a missing permission, check both the bot role and channel-specific overwrites.</li><li>If a resource was deleted, refresh the server context before publishing again.</li><li>If a provider is unavailable, pause the subscription and follow the provider status page.</li></ul>
  <p><a href="/docs/helper/troubleshooting/missing-permissions/">Missing permissions</a> · <a href="/docs/helper/troubleshooting/role-hierarchy/">Role hierarchy</a> · <a href="/docs/helper/troubleshooting/restore-configuration/">Restore configuration</a></p>
</details>

<details class="docs-reference-details"><summary>Privacy and related features</summary>
  <p>Vozen stores only the configuration and event data required by the module. Content retention, if offered, is opt-in and bounded by the server policy.</p>
  <p>Related: <a href="/docs/helper/security/privacy/">Privacy and stored data</a> · <a href="/docs/helper/status/features/">Feature status</a></p>
</details>
{% if feature.configurable %}<p><a class="button" href="https://vozen.org/panel/helper-tracker/#{{ feature.panelPath }}">Open in Helper panel</a></p>{% endif %}

